{"name":"Spanish Galleon","hex":"#817863","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spanish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To subject to spanishing, a printing process in which an ink is deposited on the bottoms and sides of depressions formed in a plastic material"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spanish"},{"term":"galleon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, three-masted, square rigged sailing ship with at least two decks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/galleon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Galleon","blocks":[{"text":"Galleons were large, multi-decked sailing ships developed in the early 16th century from ships such as the caravel and the carrack, in Portugal and in Spain. They were first used by Europeans as armed cargo carriers from the 16th to 18th centuries during the Age of Sail, and they were the principal vessels drafted for use as warships until the Anglo-Dutch Wars of the mid-17th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Padre_Eterno_em_gravura_de_1683.jpg/330px-Padre_Eterno_em_gravura_de_1683.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galleon","wikidata":"Q181469"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Cornelis_Verbeeck%2C_A_Naval_Encounter_between_Dutch_and_Spanish_Warships%2C_156252_original.jpg/500px-Cornelis_Verbeeck%2C_A_Naval_Encounter_between_Dutch_and_Spanish_Warships%2C_156252_original.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Cornelis_Verbeeck%2C_A_Naval_Encounter_between_Dutch_and_Spanish_Warships%2C_156252_original.jpg/1280px-Cornelis_Verbeeck%2C_A_Naval_Encounter_between_Dutch_and_Spanish_Warships%2C_156252_original.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Cornelis_Verbeeck%2C_A_Naval_Encounter_between_Dutch_and_Spanish_Warships%2C_156252_original.jpg/500px-Cornelis_Verbeeck%2C_A_Naval_Encounter_between_Dutch_and_Spanish_Warships%2C_156252_original.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Spanish galleon (left) firing its cannons at a Dutch warship (right). Cornelis Verbeeck, c. 1618–1620","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACornelis_Verbeeck%2C_A_Naval_Encounter_between_Dutch_and_Spanish_Warships%2C_156252_original.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Manuel_Fernandes_-_Livro_de_Tra%C3%A7as_de_Carpintaria_-_500_tonne_galleon.jpg/500px-Manuel_Fernandes_-_Livro_de_Tra%C3%A7as_de_Carpintaria_-_500_tonne_galleon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Manuel_Fernandes_-_Livro_de_Tra%C3%A7as_de_Carpintaria_-_500_tonne_galleon.jpg/1280px-Manuel_Fernandes_-_Livro_de_Tra%C3%A7as_de_Carpintaria_-_500_tonne_galleon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Manuel_Fernandes_-_Livro_de_Tra%C3%A7as_de_Carpintaria_-_500_tonne_galleon.jpg/500px-Manuel_Fernandes_-_Livro_de_Tra%C3%A7as_de_Carpintaria_-_500_tonne_galleon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Technical drawing of a late 16th century or early 17th century Portuguese galleon, featured in the Livro de Traças de Carpintaria","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManuel_Fernandes_-_Livro_de_Tra%C3%A7as_de_Carpintaria_-_500_tonne_galleon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b1/English_Galleon_Model.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b1/English_Galleon_Model.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi